<report>
<line><title>Unpaired t test</title></line>
<line></line>
<line>Mean of <in>title_0</in> = <in>mean_0</in>  (n = <in>n0</in>)</line>
<line>Mean of <in>title_1</in> = <in>mean_1</in>  (n = <in>n1</in>)</line>
<line></line>
<line><u>Assuming equal variances</u></line>
<line>Combined standard error = <in>error</in></line>
<line>df = <in>df</in></line>
<line>t =  <in>t</in></line>
<line><pval>One sided <in>p_1</in></pval></line>
<line><pval>Two sided <in>p_2</in></pval></line>
<line></line>
<line><ci><in>pc</in>% confidence interval for difference between means = <in>from</in> to <in>to</in></ci></line>
<line></line>
<line>Power <in>pwr</in></line>
<line></line>
<line><u>Assuming unequal variances</u></line>
<line>Combined standard error = <in>error_unequal</in></line>
<line>df = <in>df_unequal</in></line>
<line>t(d) =  <in>t_unequal</in></line>
<line><pval>One sided <in>p_1_unequal</in></pval></line>
<line><pval>Two sided <in>p_2_unequal</in></pval></line>
<line></line>
<line><ci><in>pc_unequal</in>% confidence interval for difference between means = <in>from_unequal</in> to <in>to_unequal</in></ci></line>
<line></line>
<line>Power <in>pwr_unequal</in></line>
<line></line>
<line><u>Comparison of variances</u></line>
<line><in>say1</in></line>
<line><in>say2</in></line>
<line></line>
<line></line>
</report>
